# Workspace agent guide

Find the workspace root by walking upwards to the nearest regular `za.toml`, including when starting inside a registered checkout or task worktree. Resolve the paths below from that root. If started in a separate checkout outside the workspace, request the workspace path when private context is needed.

## Select the scope

| Task | Context to open | Write location |
|---|---|---|
| Workspace policy, routing, integration or project registration | [Common guide](.agents/context/AGENTS.md) | Meta-repository |
| One project | Common guide, then that project's private guide below | Private context in the meta-repository; source in the active task worktree |
| Explicitly named projects | Common guide, then each named project in turn | Each change in its owning repository; coordination in common context |

Identify a project by explicit name, named path, current `.worktrees/<id>/<task-id>/`, registered checkout, then the single project in the relevant diff. Confirm registration in `.gitmodules`. If signals conflict or several candidates remain, ask which project before reading private project context. Workspace-only tasks work with zero projects.

